 ('corpses','The Empire of Corpses','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Empire_of_Corpses','Necroware-driven reanimated corpses become a major manual labor force while living people retain useful professions.','The film plot is not proof of identical novel institutions or an ordinary human welfare floor.'),
 ('doraemon','Doraemon and emotional care robots','Robert C. Marshall, Anthropology & Aging','https://anthro-age.pitt.edu/ojs/anthro-age/article/view/124','The abstract discusses a 22nd-century robot companion assisting a child.','Companion technology in the present-day household does not establish the future century’s complete economy.'),
 ('mechatopia','Doraemon: Nobita and the New Steel Troops','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doraemon%3A_Nobita_and_the_New_Steel_Troops_~Winged_Angels~','Robot classes seek human slaves; oppressed robots perform work.','The 2011 remake is identified explicitly; proposed human enslavement is not an existing supported human society.'),
